# NickelOS: the base Gentoo world every device starts with stays without Qt;
# Qt comes with the apps that need it. GnuPG's passphrase prompt is GNOME's
# (gcr, there for the keyring anyway) instead of Qt's, and AppStream comes
# without its Qt binding.
app-crypt/pinentry -qt6
dev-libs/appstream -qt6
# Sound is the session's PipeWire's (the OS's, into ChromeOS's audio
# server): Gentoo's PipeWire gives apps its libraries, without a sound
# server of its own or its settings, which the session's WirePlumber read
# too (one required Bluetooth audio).
media-video/pipewire -sound-server
